--
N5008 [basic.lookup.qual.general]/2-3: in x.eh::get() the member-qualified
name eh is looked up in the type of x, where it is a member typedef naming
the base H.  After converting x to its H subobject ([class.access.base]/6),
the front end looked up `eh::get' again in H's scope, where eh is not
visible, so f and g were left incomplete (a regression of the repeated
non-virtual base subobjects change; it dropped libstdc++'s
_Hash_code_base::_M_swap, `__x.__ebo_hash::_M_get()', in
std::unordered_map::swap).  Before that change the first three assertions
held and the repeated base A was rejected (bin53: CONVERSION ERROR).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++98), and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
